9, create filename.yml (we can create anywhere and write configurations)
10, ansible-playbook filename.yml --check (if we remove --check it will implement push configuration)

---
- hosts: droplets
  tasks:
    - name: Installs nginx web server
      apt: pkg=nginx state=installed update_cache=true
      notify:
        - start nginx

  handlers:
    - name: start nginx
      service: name=nginx state=started

---
- hosts: droplets
  tasks:
    - name: Installs nginx web server
      apt: pkg=nginx state=present update_cache=true

    - name: Upload default index.html for host
      copy: src=index.html dest=/var/www/html/index.nginx-debian.html mode=0644
      notify:
        - start nginx

  handlers:
    - name: start nginx
      service: name=nginx state=started

We can then make a directory called static_files in our current directory and place an index.html file inside.

SLAVE

1, apt-get update 
2, apt-get install python -y
3, vi /root/.ssh/authorized_keys paste id_rsa.pub
4, ifconfig copy ip and past it in master /etc/ansible/hosts

Install ansible on ubuntu 18.04 & 22.04

sudo apt-add-repository ppa:ansible/ansible
sudo apt update
sudo apt install ansible -y

Re-enable Legacy RSA Keys (Not Recommended)If you cannot upgrade your client and must use older RSA keys, you can temporarily re-enable them by adding the following lines to /etc/ssh/sshd_config via the serial console or a User Data script

HostKeyAlgorithms +ssh-rsa
PubkeyAcceptedAlgorithms +ssh-rsa

Action: Restart the service after changes: sudo systemctl restart ssh

